// Constructs that pass type and borrow checking but the IL backend does not lower yet.
// Each must be reported as E0500: the backend never compiles them to placeholder IL.
// (`()`-typed struct fields and parameters were here until tuples and `()` values landed,
// decision 52; references to references and to `()` until `Ref<T>`, decision 63.)

// An inline array cannot hold a managed pointer, nor a span view one (#43).
fn First(_refs: [&i32; 2]) {} //~ ERROR E0500 an array holding references is not yet supported by code generation

fn Second(_view: &[&i32]) {} //~ ERROR E0500 a slice of references is not yet supported by code generation

fn Main() {}
